This package is a command-oriented "scripting" tool for image data manipulation.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compilation:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
See if the executable for your machine type already exists. From Unix/Linux,
find the machine OS and architecture:

unix% uname -s
Linux
unix% uname -m
x86_64

IF THIS DIRECTORY EXISTS,
cd Linux-x86_64    (or whatever)
make
cp jip ../../bin/Linux-x86_64

IF THIS DIRECTORY DOES NOT EXIST,
mkdir Linux-x86_64 (or whatever)
cp Linx-i686/makefile Linux-x86_64
cd Linux-x86_64
make
mkdir ../../bin/Linux-x86_64
cp jip ../../bin/Linux-x86_64

REQUIRED LIBRARIES
1) jip-specific libraries:
   Go to $JIP_HOME/lib and read the file README.jip
2) NIFTI i/o library and znz library
   Go to $JIP_HOME/nifticlib-1.1.0 and read the file README.jip
3) Data compression library zlib (needed for znz libary)
   Go to $JIP_HOME/zlib-1.2.3 and read the file README.jip
4) FFTW (Fastest Fourier Transform in the West)
   go to $JIP_HOME/fftw-3.2.2 and read the file README.jip
5) Standard system libraries from /usr/lib

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Execution:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
alias xd $JIP_HOME/bin/jip   (where $JIP_HOME is the root directory)
unix% jip file.com arg1 arg2 ...
unix% jip
jip > help

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Documentation:
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This (such as it is) resides on directory $JIP_HOME/documentation.
Documentation is designed to be used from the programs.  E.g.,
"help" from the jip command line reads the file "jip-menu.txt"
on directory $JIP_HOME/documentation.
